nt, and his statement that the rider 'said ok', cannot resolve it: that statement is his own account rather than a concession, and the clause looks to the chat log. Why the AI cannot finish it. The rider's profile carries fraud_flags 1, so POL-GEN-22 requires a confidence of 0.95 for a final AI ruling. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact — here 0.85, the impaired chat log — and 0.85 is below 0.95, so the case cannot be finalised and is escalated. For the reviewer: if the message is read as agreement, the deviation is agreed and no refund is due; if it is read as an objection, the excess distance fare under POL-RD-24 is 1.30 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 0.94 SGD (the fare ledger's own figure), and the fare breakdown shows nothing yet returned (refund_issued_sgd 0.00, payment_status CHARGED). Either way, the 4.20 SGD the rider asks for is more than any row of the matrix returns, and the amount stays held until the reviewer decides."
